  "question": {
    "text": "A transparent solid cylindrical rod has a refractive index of $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$. It is surrounded by air. A light ray is incident at the mid point of one end of the rod as shown in the figure.\nThe incident angle $\\theta$ for which the light ray grazes along the wall of the rod is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/-Hl4faWAX0TwV7n9-EyB8NZT7se3PtlPfV-bvUNbNiE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SGR2Q",
      "text": "\n$\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rbpzG",
      "text": "\n$\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CYCyt",
      "text": "\n$\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1O3Dl",
      "text": "\n$\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\sin c=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\n& \\sin r=\\sin (90-c)=\\cos c=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{\\sin r}=\\frac{\\mu_2}{\\mu_1} \\\\\n& \\sin \\theta=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& \\theta=\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5lu-mk7vx8wF4Fh48k59silkWmOU_sDiF5xzBclXzEo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
